    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1989-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The numerator is \\(1 - \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{2}{3},\\) and the denominator is \\(1 - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}.\\)\n\nDividing gives \\(\\frac{2}{3} \\div \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 2 = \\frac{4}{3}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E .",
